IIMMPPLLEEMMEENNTTAATTIIOONN NNOOTTEESS
     The wwoorrddeexxpp() function is implemented using the undocumented
     ffrreeeebbssdd__wwoorrddeexxpp shell built-in command.

RREETTUURRNN VVAALLUUEESS
     The wwoorrddeexxpp() function returns zero if successful, otherwise it returns
     one of the following error codes:

     WRDE_BADCHAR  The _w_o_r_d_s argument contains one of the following unquoted
                   characters: ⟨newline⟩, ‘|’, ‘&’, ‘;’, ‘<’, ‘>’, ‘(’, ‘)’,
                   ‘{’, ‘}’.

     WRDE_BADVAL   An error after successful parsing, such as an attempt to
                   expand an undefined shell variable with WRDE_UNDEF set in
                   _f_l_a_g_s.

     WRDE_CMDSUB   An attempt was made to use command substitution and
                   WRDE_NOCMD is set in _f_l_a_g_s.

     WRDE_NOSPACE  Not enough memory to store the result or an error during
                   fork(2).

     WRDE_SYNTAX   Shell syntax error in _w_o_r_d_s.

     The wwoorrddffrreeee() function returns no value.

